Cross-border networks optimized for cost are now exposed to tariff swings, sanctions and customs delays that can change in a single news cycle.

## Dual-Source the Critical Few

Not every component needs a second source. The handful that would halt production do, and qualifying them early is far cheaper than doing it during a disruption.

## Model Landed Cost Continuously

Re-running landed-cost models monthly, instead of annually, lets procurement act on tariff changes while alternatives are still available.
